3
00:00:10.406 --> 00:00:17.500
The OpenGL graphics pipeline processes
vertices through programmable shader stages.

4
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:24.944
Consider this worked case: A triangle mesh is
passed to vertex shaders that compute position

5
00:00:24.944 --> 00:00:27.921
and normal attributes for each vertex.

6
00:00:27.921 --> 00:00:34.877
List the givens before choosing a method,
because an unstated assumption can change the

7
00:00:34.877 --> 00:00:35.374
conclusion.

8
00:00:35.374 --> 00:00:41.531
This establishes the vocabulary and scope
needed for the remaining sections.

9
00:00:41.642 --> 00:00:48.714
Now define Primitive Assembly and Clipping
precisely enough that another learner could

10
00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:50.482
